H%2FJrhBlEHQFSKA%3D%3D","c":"45"}],"q":null,"nivel":"insuficiente"}},"entidad":{"id":"ES0611001I","nombre":"Junta de Extremadura"},"hash":"48a78b5e8740b6ab","ia":{"es":"Qué muestran los datos: Entre 2023 y 2025, este organismo adjudicó 53 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 10,8 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 4,9, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,3 a 7,3. En diciembre se adjudicó el 2 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 6 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 40 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.292,86 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a razones legales, como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No implica que se haya violado el límite ni que haya existido mala fe.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o fechas específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 53 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 10.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.9, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.3 to 7.3. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,292.86 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper actions. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove misconduct or errors in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contract details for [1] to see what was purchased and the reason for the amount. Review awardee A’s contracts to identify if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Look for patterns in the timing of awards to determine if contracts were rushed or planned in advance.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["gONAovOh0oXs%2BnLj3vAg5A%3D%3D","i84JsFSwl3jVGIpKDxgsAQ%3D%3D","tMtTtzP98rryoM4us5k4vw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}